Hi Lorenzo,

So it turns out that the revisitation distribution is proportional to the the speed-weighted average of the joint distribution of both position and velocity, whereas the utilization distribution derives from the uniformly-weighted average. The derivations are in an upcoming book.

That in mind, you could run an SSF and look for selection for landcover + an interaction between step-length and landcover. That basically gets at what you want.

Best,
Chris

