Hi Alex,

Usually you get problems if all of the data is in one category or something like that -- if that's not the case, then please send me a minimal working example and I'll take a look at it.

When you change the reference category, the coefficients should change in a consistent way. You can think of the beta for category A with reference category B as beta[A|B] = beta[A] - beta[B].
So if you switch to reference category C, then beta[A|C]  will be different from beta[A|B], but you should have beta[A|B] = beta[A|C] - beta[B|C] and you should also have beta[C|B] = -beta[B|C].

Best,
Chris

